      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good overview. I'm seeing some weird data in the telemetry though. During the third or fourth heavy braking cycle, the semi-metallic pads seem to behave inconsistently—it's like the heat is causing some unpredictable, almost erratic friction fluctuations instead of a smooth decay. Is there a specific mechanical reason why the thermal gradient would cause that kind of erratic behavior in the material, or is it just standard noise?",
